            type: "text",
            id: "c-l31-b2",
            body: 'The alt attribute is a replacement for the image, not a description of it. It is what a screen reader announces in place of the image, and it is what appears when the image fails to load. Write it as a short phrase, with no "image of" or "picture of" at the start \u2014 the reader already announced the element type. If the text is long enough to need a sentence or two, it belongs in a `figcaption` next to the image, not in the alt attribute.'
