            body: "A `<canvas>` is a rectangular drawing surface. It has no content of its own \u2014 the fallback inside the tags is what a browser shows when it cannot render canvas, and that is the only content the element has. Everything drawn on it is drawn by script through a context object obtained from `getContext`. The canvas knows nothing about what is on it, which is the single most important thing to remember about it."
