            body: "`new Date()` means now. `new Date(1750000000000)` takes that number as epoch milliseconds, so a large number like `new Date(2026, 0, 15)` is not one call at all \u2014 it is the multi-argument form, and the brackets are how the arguments get separated. When you only want the number, `Date.now()` gives it without building the object. A single subtraction between `Date.now()` before and after some work is also how you time a piece of code."
