            type: "tip",
            id: "j-l41-t1",
            title: "When a class earns its place",
            body: 'Reach for a plain object when it is one set of related values, or a function you hand data to. Reach for a class when each thing carries its **own state** \u2014 a counter, an id, a done flag \u2014 *and* has behaviour that acts on that state, especially when you will make more than one. Two tests: if the "class" will only ever have a single instance, it is probably a module; if a method never touches `this`, it does not need to be a method.'
