            body: "A **getter** is a function that runs when you read a property; a **setter** runs when you write one. Neither takes the value as an argument in the usual sense: the setter always gets exactly one, the value assigned. Together they let a property keep an invariant \u2014 that is, a promise that whatever is stored inside is always in a usable state."
