            body: "`Object.keys` and `for\u2026of` see own properties only. A plain read walks the chain, which is why `t.hasOwnProperty` works even though nothing in your code ever put that method on `t`. The console shows this as `__proto__`, and it is a debugging aid rather than something to write in application code \u2014 use `Object.getPrototypeOf(t)` instead."
