            type: "warning",
            id: "j-l73-w1",
            title: "firstChild is usually whitespace",
            body: "Reach for `firstElementChild`, or index `children`, not `firstChild`. `firstChild` is the very first node in the parent, which in any normally formatted markup is the indentation before the first tag \u2014 a text node whose `textContent` is a string of spaces. The fix is not to strip the whitespace; it is to stop looking at nodes when you meant elements."
