            type: "text",
            id: "j-l74-b3",
            body: '`append` is the one to reach for: it takes nodes *and* plain strings, so `list.append("Tea")` and `list.append(li)` are both legal, and it returns nothing. `appendChild` is the older sibling that only accepts nodes and returns the node it added \u2014 which is occasionally handy, and mostly a trap if you assume every method returns something.'
