            body: "The Geolocation API gives JavaScript access to the device physical location through navigator.geolocation.getCurrentPosition. It is gated behind a permission prompt the browser shows on the first call, and the user can deny it at any time. The API never gives you an exact address \u2014 it gives you latitude, longitude, accuracy, and optional heading and speed \u2014 and it only works over HTTPS, because location is considered sensitive."
